@node Overview
@chapter Overview

@samp{sgn} is a full-featured Signal messenger client for Emacs@comma{} designed to replace Signal Desktop for daily use.  It communicates with a running @samp{signal-cli} daemon via JSON-RPC and persists all message history locally in an SQLite database with full-text search. @*

The user experience is modeled after @samp{telega}@comma{} the Telegram client for Emacs.  Chat buffers use a header-plus-body grouping style@comma{} with text properties on every message enabling point-based commands for reactions@comma{} replies@comma{} editing@comma{} deletion@comma{} and more.  A dashboard buffer provides a chat list with unread badges@comma{} last-message previews@comma{} and pinned chats. @*

Received data flows in one direction.  @samp{signal-cli} delivers each incoming envelope as a JSON-RPC notification; @samp{sgn-event.el} turns it into a list of events; @samp{sgn-store.el} applies those events to the database in a single transaction and then reports which chats changed.  Chat buffers@comma{} the dashboard and the unread indicator never patch themselves: they redraw from the database when the store tells them to.  Actions you take@comma{} such as sending@comma{} reacting or deleting@comma{} go out through @samp{sgn-actions.el} and record their outcome in the database the same way. @*

The package is split into focused modules: @*

@itemize
@item
@samp{sgn.el} --- Entry point@comma{} user options@comma{} session lifecycle@comma{} and the glue between the other modules. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-rpc.el} --- JSON-RPC subprocess management@comma{} request bookkeeping@comma{} and failure reporting. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-event.el} --- Normalizes @samp{signal-cli} envelopes into events. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-store.el} --- Applies events to the database in one transaction and runs the change hooks. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-db.el} --- SQLite persistence layer with FTS5 full-text search@comma{} schema migrations@comma{} and identity merging. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-chat.el} --- Chat buffer mode: rendering from the database@comma{} the input area@comma{} drafts@comma{} and typing indicators. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-actions.el} --- Sending and message actions: send@comma{} attach@comma{} react@comma{} reply@comma{} edit@comma{} delete@comma{} forward@comma{} pin@comma{} and chat settings. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-contacts.el} --- Contact/group name cache and completing-read interface. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-media.el} --- Inline images@comma{} stickers@comma{} attachments@comma{} and voice note playback. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-format.el} --- Text formatting: render Signal styles and mentions@comma{} parse and reconstruct markup. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-notify.el} --- Modeline/tab-bar unread indicator and desktop notifications. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-search.el} --- FTS5-powered search across conversations. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-dashboard.el} --- Chat list buffer with sorting@comma{} unread tracking@comma{} and fade-out truncation. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-import.el} --- Import of text message history from Signal Desktop. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-link.el} --- Linking @samp{signal-cli} to a Signal account as a secondary device. @*
@end itemize

People are identified by their ACI@comma{} the UUID Signal assigns to each account.  A phone number is only used until the ACI is known: when the contact list or an incoming envelope reveals both@comma{} everything stored under the number (the chat@comma{} messages@comma{} reactions@comma{} receipts and pins) is rewritten to the ACI@comma{} and duplicate copies of a message are merged (@ref{Database operations, , Database operations}).  Groups are identified by their base64 group ID@.  A message is identified by its chat@comma{} its sender@comma{} and the timestamp Signal assigned to it. @*

The database is at schema version 3.  A database written by an earlier version of @samp{sgn} (version 1 or 2) is migrated automatically by @code{sgn-start}@comma{} after a snapshot of it is saved in the @samp{backups} subdirectory of @code{sgn-db-directory}.  Version 2 kept only a per-chat unread count@comma{} so after migration the newest that many incoming messages of each chat remain unread; read messages with a disappearing timer start counting down.  A database written by a newer @samp{sgn} is refused with an error. @*

@strong{Prerequisites}: @*

@enumerate
@item
Emacs 29.1 or later@comma{} compiled with SQLite and FTS5 support. @*
@item
@samp{signal-cli} v0.14+ installed and in @code{$PATH}@comma{} with a registered or linked Signal account. @*
@item
Optional: an audio player listed in @code{sgn-audio-players} (@samp{mpv}@comma{} @samp{ffplay} or @samp{afplay}) for voice notes; @samp{sqlcipher} CLI (and@comma{} on macOS@comma{} @samp{node}) for Signal Desktop import; @samp{qrencode} for showing the linking QR code in @code{sgn-link}. @*
@end enumerate

The package has no external Emacs package dependencies --- it uses only built-in libraries. @*

The development repository is on @uref{https://github.com/benthamite/sgn, GitHub}. @*

