@node Keymaps
@section Keymaps

@vindex sgn-chat-mode-map
@vindex sgn-chat-message-map
@vindex sgn-dashboard-mode-map
@vindex sgn-search-mode-map
The keymap @code{sgn-chat-mode-map} is active everywhere in a chat buffer.  It binds @samp{RET} to @code{sgn-chat-return}@comma{} @samp{S-<return>} and @samp{C-j} to @code{newline}@comma{} @samp{C-c C-a} to @code{sgn-attach-file}@comma{} @samp{C-c C-s} to @code{sgn-search-in-chat}@comma{} @samp{C-c C-l} to @code{sgn-load-more-history}@comma{} and @samp{C-g} to @code{sgn-chat-cancel-action}. @*

The keymap @code{sgn-chat-message-map} holds the single-key commands for the message at point (@ref{Message actions, , Message actions}).  It is attached to each rendered message through the @samp{keymap} text property@comma{} so its keys are active only when point is on a message; in the input area the same keys insert text. @*

The keymap @code{sgn-dashboard-mode-map} holds the dashboard bindings (@ref{Dashboard, , Dashboard})@comma{} and @code{sgn-search-mode-map} the bindings of the search results buffer (@ref{Searching, , Searching}). @*

@node Hooks
@section Hooks

@vindex sgn-store-changed-functions
@vindex sgn-store-new-message-functions
@vindex sgn-store-typing-functions
@vindex sgn-db-merge-functions
@vindex sgn-rpc-receive-handler
@vindex sgn-rpc-failure-change-hook
These hooks connect the store and the RPC layer to the user interface.  @samp{sgn.el} installs the functions that keep chat buffers@comma{} the dashboard and the indicator up to date; you can add your own to react to the same events.  The functions run after the database transaction has been committed@comma{} so they can read the new state. @*

The abnormal hook @code{sgn-store-changed-functions} is called with a list of chat IDs whose stored state changed: new or edited messages@comma{} reactions@comma{} receipts@comma{} pins@comma{} read state@comma{} names@comma{} or settings.  @code{sgn-chat-on-store-changed}@comma{} @code{sgn-dashboard-on-store-changed} and @code{sgn-notify-on-store-changed} are on it by default. @*

The abnormal hook @code{sgn-store-new-message-functions} is called with the chat ID and rowid of each newly stored incoming message@comma{} once per message.  Messages sent from this account@comma{} including those sent from your other devices@comma{} are not reported here.  By default it marks the chat read if you are looking at it@comma{} and otherwise queues a desktop notification and@comma{} if @code{sgn-auto-open-buffer} is non-nil@comma{} displays the chat. @*

The abnormal hook @code{sgn-store-typing-functions} is called with a chat ID@comma{} a sender@comma{} and a flag that is non-nil if the sender started typing and @code{nil} if they stopped.  By default @code{sgn-chat-on-typing} shows the indicator in the chat's header line. @*

The abnormal hook @code{sgn-db-merge-functions} is called with a phone number and the ACI it was just merged into.  By default @code{sgn-chat-on-identity-merged} moves a chat buffer opened under the number to the ACI@comma{} so that a chat started by typing a number keeps its buffer once the contact replies. @*

The variable @code{sgn-rpc-receive-handler} holds the function called with the parameters of each @samp{receive} notification from @samp{signal-cli}.  @code{sgn-start} sets it to a function that passes the envelope through @code{sgn-event-from-envelope} and @code{sgn-store-apply}. @*

The normal hook @code{sgn-rpc-failure-change-hook} runs whenever the recorded @samp{signal-cli} failure is set or cleared (@ref{Starting and stopping, , Starting and stopping}); by default it updates the indicator and the dashboard. @*

@node Buffer-local state
@section Buffer-local state

@vindex sgn-chat-id
The buffer-local variable @code{sgn-chat-id} holds the chat ID of a chat buffer: a person's ACI (or phone number@comma{} while the ACI is unknown) or a group's base64 ID@.  Commands that act on ``the current chat''@comma{} such as @code{sgn-attach-file}@comma{} @code{sgn-search-in-chat} and @code{sgn-set-disappearing}@comma{} read it and signal an error when it is @code{nil}. @*

