@node Session and read state
@section Session and read state

@findex sgn-running-p
@findex sgn-ensure-running
@findex sgn-mark-chat-read
@findex sgn-link-in-progress-p
@findex sgn-import-desktop-available-p
The function @code{sgn-running-p} returns non-nil if the database is open and @samp{signal-cli} is running. @*

The function @code{sgn-ensure-running} starts @samp{sgn} unless @samp{signal-cli} is running.  If @samp{signal-cli} has failed@comma{} it signals that failure@comma{} with the command that fixes it@comma{} instead of starting it again.  Commands that send anything call it first. @*

The function @code{sgn-mark-chat-read} marks every unread message of a chat as read@comma{} starting the countdown of those with a disappearing timer@comma{} and sends read receipts to their senders when @code{sgn-send-read-receipts} is non-nil and @samp{signal-cli} is running.  It is called when a chat becomes visible in a focused frame and by @code{sgn-dashboard-mark-read}. @*

The function @code{sgn-link-in-progress-p} returns non-nil while @code{sgn-link} is linking.  The function @code{sgn-import-desktop-available-p} returns non-nil if a Signal Desktop database and the @samp{sqlcipher} program are available. @*

@node Contact resolution
@section Contact resolution

@findex sgn-contacts-get-name
@findex sgn-contacts-set-name
@findex sgn-contacts-name-known-p
@findex sgn-contacts-display-sender
@findex sgn-contacts-completing-read
@findex sgn-contacts-load-from-db
@findex sgn-contacts-start-refresh-timer
@findex sgn-contacts-stop-refresh-timer
@findex sgn-contacts-format-time
The function @code{sgn-contacts-get-name} returns the display name for a person or group ID@.  For this account it returns @samp{"Note to Self"}.  Without a cached name@comma{} it falls back to the person's phone number if known@comma{} to ``Unknown'' followed by the first eight characters of an ACI@comma{} or to the ID itself. @*

The function @code{sgn-contacts-set-name} stores a display name for an ID in the in-memory cache; empty names are ignored.  The function @code{sgn-contacts-name-known-p} returns non-nil if a name is cached for an ID@. @*

The function @code{sgn-contacts-display-sender} returns a display string for a message sender: @samp{"You"} for this account@comma{} and otherwise the result of @code{sgn-contacts-get-name}. @*

The function @code{sgn-contacts-completing-read} presents the @code{completing-read} interface used by @code{sgn-chat} (@ref{Opening chats, , Opening chats}) and returns the selected chat ID@comma{} not the display name.  Its optional arguments are a PROMPT (default @samp{"Chat: "}) and ALLOW-EMPTY@comma{} which makes empty input return @code{nil}; @code{sgn-create-group} uses the latter to end its member list.  A phone number is returned as the ACI recorded for it@comma{} if any. @*

The function @code{sgn-contacts-load-from-db} fills the in-memory name cache from the recipients and chats stored in the database.  @code{sgn-start} calls it.  The functions @code{sgn-contacts-start-refresh-timer} and @code{sgn-contacts-stop-refresh-timer} start and stop the periodic @code{sgn-contacts-refresh}. @*

The function @code{sgn-contacts-format-time} formats a millisecond timestamp for chat lists: the time for today@comma{} the weekday for this week@comma{} and the date otherwise.  With its optional argument WITH-TIME@comma{} weekdays and dates include the time; this is the @code{smart} format of @code{sgn-timestamp-format}. @*

@node Chat buffer management
@section Chat buffer management

@findex sgn-chat-buffer
@findex sgn-chat-get-buffer
@findex sgn-chat-buffers
@findex sgn-chat-open
@findex sgn-chat-schedule-redraw
@findex sgn-chat-on-store-changed
@findex sgn-chat-show-message
@findex sgn-chat-on-typing
@findex sgn-chat-visible-p
@findex sgn-chat-message-at-point
@findex sgn-chat-start-reply
@findex sgn-chat-start-edit
@findex sgn-chat-save-all-drafts
@findex sgn-chat-format-duration
The function @code{sgn-chat-buffer} returns the live buffer of a chat ID from the buffer registry@comma{} or @code{nil}.  The function @code{sgn-chat-get-buffer} returns it@comma{} creating it if necessary: a new buffer is named @samp{*sgn: <display-name>*} (with a numeric suffix if another buffer already has that name)@comma{} draws its prompt@comma{} restores the chat's draft@comma{} and draws the history.  The function @code{sgn-chat-buffers} returns all live chat buffers. @*

The function @code{sgn-chat-open} ensures the chat exists in the database and shows its buffer in the selected window.  Showing it marks the chat read if the frame has focus (@ref{Messaging behavior, , Messaging behavior}). @*

The function @code{sgn-chat-schedule-redraw} redraws a chat's buffer@comma{} if it has one@comma{} once the current command is done; several requests before then cause a single redraw.  The function @code{sgn-chat-on-store-changed} calls it for each chat ID it receives@comma{} as a member of @code{sgn-store-changed-functions} (@ref{Hooks, , Hooks}). @*

The function @code{sgn-chat-show-message} moves point to a message given its rowid@comma{} in the current chat buffer@comma{} raising the number of messages shown if the message is older than those drawn.  @code{sgn-search-goto-result} uses it. @*

The function @code{sgn-chat-on-typing} shows or hides@comma{} in the header line of the chat's buffer@comma{} that a sender is typing.  An indicator that is not renewed disappears after fifteen seconds.  It is a member of @code{sgn-store-typing-functions}. @*

The function @code{sgn-chat-visible-p} returns non-nil if a chat's buffer is in the selected window of a focused frame@comma{} which is the condition for counting its messages as read. @*

The function @code{sgn-chat-message-at-point} returns the database record of the message at point as a plist@comma{} with keys such as @code{:rowid}@comma{} @code{:chat-id}@comma{} @code{:sender}@comma{} @code{:timestamp}@comma{} @code{:outgoing}@comma{} @code{:body}@comma{} @code{:styles-json}@comma{} @code{:deleted} and @code{:send-status}@comma{} or @code{nil}.  This is the foundation for all point-based message actions (@ref{Message actions, , Message actions}). @*

The functions @code{sgn-chat-start-reply} and @code{sgn-chat-start-edit} put the current chat buffer in reply or edit mode for a message plist; the latter also fills the input with the given text.  @code{sgn-reply} and @code{sgn-edit} call them. @*

The function @code{sgn-chat-save-all-drafts} saves the input of every chat buffer as its chat's draft.  @code{sgn-stop} and Emacs's exit call it. @*

The function @code{sgn-chat-format-duration} formats a number of seconds as a short duration such as @samp{"5m"} or @samp{"7d"}@comma{} as shown for disappearing timers. @*

@node Sending functions
@section Sending functions

@findex sgn-send-text
@findex sgn-send-edit
@findex sgn-chat-address
@findex sgn-actions-result-status
The function @code{sgn-send-text} sends a text@comma{} which may contain markup (@ref{Text formatting, , Text formatting})@comma{} to a chat ID; its optional third argument@comma{} a message plist@comma{} makes it a reply.  The message is stored and shown at once with send status @samp{sending}@comma{} and its status is then updated as described in @ref{Sending messages and media, , Sending messages and media}.  It returns the new message's rowid.  This is the function behind @code{sgn-chat-send-input}@comma{} and it can be called from Lisp to send messages programmatically. @*

The function @code{sgn-send-edit} replaces the text of a message you sent@comma{} given as a message plist@comma{} with new text that may contain markup.  The new text is shown at once@comma{} labelled @emph{saving edit…}@comma{} and restored if @samp{signal-cli} rejects the edit.  An edit that @samp{signal-cli} does not confirm within @code{sgn-send-timeout} seconds@comma{} or that is interrupted by a restart@comma{} is labelled @emph{edit not confirmed}; the message itself keeps counting as sent.  While you compose an edit@comma{} the text you were typing is set aside and comes back when the edit is sent or cancelled. @*

The function @code{sgn-chat-address} returns the RPC parameters addressing a chat ID: a @samp{groupId} for groups@comma{} and otherwise a @samp{recipient}@comma{} using @code{sgn-account} for Note to Self. @*

The function @code{sgn-actions-result-status} returns the send status for the result of a @samp{signal-cli} @samp{send} request: @samp{"sent"} when every recipient succeeded@comma{} @samp{"failed"} when none did@comma{} and @samp{"partial"} otherwise. @*

@node Event normalization
@section Event normalization

@findex sgn-event-from-envelope
The function @code{sgn-event-from-envelope} returns the events in the parameters of a @samp{signal-cli} @samp{receive} notification.  Its second argument identifies this account and is used as the sender of messages sent from your other devices.  Each event is a plist with a @code{:kind} key; the kinds are @code{contact} (an envelope's ACI@comma{} number and profile name)@comma{} @code{group} (a group's name)@comma{} @code{message}@comma{} @code{edit}@comma{} @code{delete}@comma{} @code{reaction}@comma{} @code{pin} (including unpins)@comma{} @code{timer} (a disappearing timer change)@comma{} @code{read} (a read sync from another device)@comma{} @code{receipt} (delivered@comma{} read or viewed)@comma{} and @code{typing}.  People are identified by ACI@comma{} falling back to the phone number when @samp{signal-cli} reports no ACI@comma{} and style and mention offsets are kept in UTF-16 code units.  An incoming poll becomes a @code{message} whose body is @samp{📊} followed by the question.  The function only transforms data; it neither reads nor writes the database. @*

@node Event store
@section Event store

@findex sgn-store-apply
@findex sgn-store-changed
@findex sgn-store-delete-content
@findex sgn-store-purge-expired
@findex sgn-store-self
@findex sgn-store-self-p
@findex sgn-store-self-ids
@findex sgn-store-learn-self
@findex sgn-store-load-self
The function @code{sgn-store-apply} stores a list of events@comma{} as returned by @code{sgn-event-from-envelope}@comma{} in a single database transaction@comma{} and then runs @code{sgn-store-changed-functions}@comma{} @code{sgn-store-new-message-functions} and @code{sgn-store-typing-functions} to report what changed (@ref{Hooks, , Hooks}).  A message already stored is not stored again.  Edits@comma{} remote deletes and read syncs whose message has not arrived yet are kept in a @samp{pending} table and applied when it arrives; pending entries older than thirty days are dropped by @code{sgn-start}.  A remote delete only applies to a message by the same sender@comma{} and an edit only replaces the text if it is newer than the last edit applied. @*

The function @code{sgn-store-changed} reports that the stored state of the given chat IDs changed.  While @code{sgn-store-apply} is running@comma{} the chats are collected and reported once at the end; otherwise @code{sgn-store-changed-functions} runs at once.  Code outside the store that writes to the database calls it so that the interface redraws. @*

The function @code{sgn-store-delete-content} deletes a message's text and attachment files@comma{} keeping a @samp{[Message deleted]} tombstone.  The function @code{sgn-store-purge-expired} deletes@comma{} attachments included@comma{} every message whose disappearing timer has run out; @code{sgn-start} schedules it every ten seconds. @*

The function @code{sgn-store-self} returns the identifier of this account: its ACI once known@comma{} and @code{sgn-account} until then.  @code{sgn-store-self-p} returns non-nil if an ID identifies this account by either form@comma{} and @code{sgn-store-self-ids} returns both forms.  @code{sgn-store-learn-self} records the account's ACI@comma{} saving it in the database and merging data stored under @code{sgn-account} into it; @code{sgn-store-load-self} loads the saved ACI at startup. @*

@node Database operations
@section Database operations

@findex sgn-db-init
@findex sgn-db-close
@findex sgn-db-backup
@findex sgn-db-select
@findex sgn-db-select-value
@findex sgn-db-execute
@findex sgn-db-with-transaction
@findex sgn-db-now
The function @code{sgn-db-init} opens the SQLite database in @code{sgn-db-directory}.  It creates the directory if needed@comma{} verifies SQLite and FTS5 support@comma{} enables WAL journaling and foreign keys@comma{} and creates the schema in a new database or migrates an older one to version 3 (@ref{Overview, , Overview}).  Called by @code{sgn-start}.  The function @code{sgn-db-close} closes the connection.  The function @code{sgn-db-backup} writes a consistent snapshot of the open database to a file@comma{} using SQLite's @samp{VACUUM INTO}; this is a safe way to copy the database while @samp{sgn} runs. @*

The functions @code{sgn-db-select}@comma{} @code{sgn-db-select-value} and @code{sgn-db-execute} run an SQL statement with optional parameters@comma{} returning respectively all rows@comma{} the first column of the first row@comma{} and the number of changed rows.  Unlike plain @code{sqlite-select}@comma{} they signal SQLite errors rather than silently returning no rows@comma{} and they signal an error if the database is not open. @*

The macro @code{sgn-db-with-transaction} runs its body in a database transaction@comma{} which is committed if the body returns normally and rolled back if it signals an error.  Nested uses join the outermost transaction.  The function @code{sgn-db-now} returns the current time in milliseconds since the epoch@comma{} the unit of all stored timestamps. @*

