@node Request helpers
@subsection Request helpers

@findex sgn-rpc-address
@findex sgn-rpc-send-message
@findex sgn-rpc-send-reaction
@findex sgn-rpc-send-typing
@findex sgn-rpc-send-receipt
@findex sgn-rpc-remote-delete
@findex sgn-rpc-send-pin
@findex sgn-rpc-list-contacts
@findex sgn-rpc-list-groups
These functions build the parameters of specific @samp{signal-cli} methods and pass them to @code{sgn-rpc-send}.  They take an ADDRESS@comma{} the alist returned by @code{sgn-rpc-address} (a @samp{groupId} for a group@comma{} a @samp{recipient} otherwise) or by @code{sgn-chat-address}. @*

The function @code{sgn-rpc-send-message} sends a text to an address@comma{} with optional extra @samp{send} parameters such as @samp{quoteTimestamp}@comma{} @samp{attachments}@comma{} @samp{textStyle} or @samp{editTimestamp}@comma{} and optional callbacks; the result's @samp{timestamp} is the message's Signal timestamp.  @code{sgn-rpc-send-reaction} sends or removes a reaction to the message an author sent at a timestamp.  @code{sgn-rpc-remote-delete} deletes one of your messages for everyone@comma{} and @code{sgn-rpc-send-pin} pins or unpins a message. @*

The functions @code{sgn-rpc-send-typing} and @code{sgn-rpc-send-receipt} send a typing indicator and a receipt (@samp{"read"} by default); their failures are only logged.  @code{sgn-rpc-list-contacts} and @code{sgn-rpc-list-groups} request the contact and group lists and pass them to a callback. @*

@node Media rendering (1)
@section Media rendering

@findex sgn-media-render
@findex sgn-media-path
@findex sgn-media-find-sticker
@findex sgn-media-delete-files
@findex sgn-media-open
@findex sgn-media-play-audio
The database stores what @samp{signal-cli} reports about each attachment (its ID@comma{} type and name)@comma{} not a path; the path is worked out when the message is drawn.  A sticker or attachment that @samp{signal-cli} downloads later therefore shows up on the next redraw. @*

The function @code{sgn-media-render} inserts a line showing a media plist in a chat buffer: an inline image (respecting @code{sgn-image-max-width} or@comma{} for stickers@comma{} @code{sgn-sticker-max-width}@comma{} and animated when @code{sgn-enable-animation} is non-nil)@comma{} a @samp{🎤 Voice note} button@comma{} or a @samp{[File: NAME]} link.  Missing files show as @samp{[Media not downloaded]} or @samp{[Sticker]}@comma{} and a rendering error inserts a placeholder rather than interrupting the redraw. @*

The function @code{sgn-media-path} returns the file holding a media plist@comma{} or @code{nil} if it is absent: the file's own path for attachments sent from Emacs@comma{} the sticker file for stickers@comma{} and otherwise the file named by the attachment ID inside the @samp{attachments} directory of @code{sgn-data-directory}.  Since attachment IDs come from the network@comma{} an ID containing a slash is rejected.  @code{sgn-media-find-sticker} locates the file for a sticker by pack ID and sticker ID@comma{} using the pack's @samp{manifest.json} if present and the numeric ID as the file name otherwise. @*

The function @code{sgn-media-delete-files} deletes the files @samp{signal-cli} stored for a list of media plists@comma{} leaving files sent from Emacs and stickers alone. @*

The function @code{sgn-media-open} opens a file with the system's default application.  The function @code{sgn-media-play-audio} plays an audio file with the first program found in @code{sgn-audio-players}@comma{} or stops the voice note playing if one is; if the player exits with an error@comma{} it says so. @*

@node Text formatting (1)
@section Text formatting

@findex sgn-format-render
@findex sgn-format-parse-markup
@findex sgn-format-to-markup
@findex sgn-format-preview
@findex sgn-format-read-ranges
@findex sgn-format-ranges-to-json
@findex sgn-format-utf16-to-char
@findex sgn-format-char-to-utf16
Styles and mentions are represented as lists of ranges @samp{(NAME START LENGTH)}@comma{} where NAME is a style (BOLD@comma{} ITALIC@comma{} STRIKETHROUGH@comma{} MONOSPACE or SPOILER) or a mentioned person's ID@comma{} and START and LENGTH are in UTF-16 code units. @*

The function @code{sgn-format-render} returns a message body with its style ranges and mention ranges applied.  Each style is mapped to a face (@ref{Text formatting faces, , Text formatting faces}); spoiler text additionally receives the @code{sgn-spoiler} text property and stays concealed unless the optional REVEALED argument is non-nil.  Mentions are replaced by @samp{@@} followed by the person's display name. @*

The function @code{sgn-format-parse-markup} parses lightweight markup in user input@comma{} following the rules in @ref{Text formatting, , Text formatting}.  It returns a plist with @code{:text} (the plain text with delimiters removed) and @code{:styles} (a list of style ranges).  The function @code{sgn-format-to-markup} does the reverse for editing: it writes a body's styles back as markup and escapes delimiter characters that would otherwise be read as markup@comma{} so that parsing the result gives back the same text and styles. @*

The function @code{sgn-format-preview} returns a message's text on one line@comma{} with mentions resolved and spoiler characters replaced by @samp{▒}@comma{} for the dashboard and notifications. @*

The functions @code{sgn-format-read-ranges} and @code{sgn-format-ranges-to-json} convert range lists from and to the JSON stored in the database; the former also reads the object form written by older versions.  @code{sgn-format-utf16-to-char} and @code{sgn-format-char-to-utf16} convert between UTF-16 offsets and character positions in a string. @*

@node Notification helpers
@section Notification helpers

@findex sgn-notify-update
@findex sgn-notify-on-store-changed
@findex sgn-notify-message
The function @code{sgn-notify-update} recounts the unread messages in the database and updates the modeline or tab-bar indicator.  Muted chats are excluded from the count.  The function @code{sgn-notify-on-store-changed} calls it as a member of @code{sgn-store-changed-functions}. @*

The function @code{sgn-notify-message} queues a desktop notification for a new message@comma{} given its chat ID and rowid@comma{} unless notifications are disabled or the chat is muted.  About a second later@comma{} the queued messages of each chat are announced in a single notification@comma{} leaving out those read in the meantime (@ref{Notifications, , Notifications}). @*

@node Dashboard functions
@section Dashboard functions

@findex sgn-dashboard-on-store-changed
The function @code{sgn-dashboard-on-store-changed} schedules a refresh of the dashboard once the current command is done@comma{} as a member of @code{sgn-store-changed-functions}.  Several changes before then cause a single refresh@comma{} which keeps point and each window on the same chat. @*

